Upstream models

Sample Trail sends a recording, an image or a piece of text to a model endpoint that you configure
and hold the key for. The lab does not train, fine-tune or distribute models, and is not a provider
of a general-purpose AI model under the EU AI Act; obligations for the model itself rest with
whoever provides it, under their own terms.

A model is used for exactly one bounded job: reading a quality evaluation into the named values the
contract spec asks about, with a confidence on each. No model produces a pass or a fail. Verdicts
come from a deterministic comparison against thresholds held in a spreadsheet, and swapping the
model cannot change one.

Output produced through that endpoint is marked per Article 50. See COMPLIANCE.md.

---

Scope

Sample Trail runs the approval decision on a physical commodity sample and keeps the record of it.
It is not a laboratory information management system, it is not a traceability system, and it does
not know whether the thresholds you put in it are the right ones for your contract.
